  "notes": "Generic curtain, not a specific product: one panel of a light blue linen curtain on a ceiling track, pulled open to the side of a window, where it gathers into a stack of wave folds with a hem and a heading tape. Place it beside a window: like other floor items it snaps flush and square to the wall, also to the angled glazing walls, and its folds keep 3 cm off it. It stands on the floor so it can snap to the wall and reaches the ceiling with its track (255 cm, the apartment's ceiling height); the cloth ends 1.5 cm above the floor. It is one panel, 36.4 cm wide and 15.5 cm deep including the gap at the back: duplicate it for the other side of the window. Only the folds collide, not the gap behind them. Unlined light blue linen (curtain.linen-light-blue), the light blue of the armchairs: like real unlined linen it lets some daylight through (opacity 0.8), which shows its folds against the window; for a fully opaque curtain pick one of the fabric presets. Any curtain or fabric preset can be picked."
